A person signs in, and the store works out what they may do
A clinician signs in at the tenant's own authority. The authority reads the
tenant's records to find the person and a role whose period has not ended,
and issues a token naming the capacity it resolved. The clinician then
presents that token to the face, which checks what the capacity allows
against the same records and answers with that and no more. Revoking access
is ending a period on the role record; there is no second user directory to
change.
